ion this includes  tax fraud insurance fraud  falsification of business records and a  whole bunch of other stuff now before  looking at the details  a grand jury looking at a former  president is a huge deal it's enormous  uh and we have to understand that we're  gonna  look at some things that former  prosecutor renato marriotti said and  we're going to talk about you know is  trump likely to ever go to prison the  answer is no  but consider the sort of you know the  you  the boiling frog in the skillet you  slowly turn up the temperature  it doesn't notice that it's getting  burned consider how far we've come  where as asha rangapa said on twitter  before the presidency the access  hollywood grab him by the you know what  tape oh my goodness this is crazy this  is the craziest thing we've ever seen  we have a grand jury now considering  indictments of a former president  and it didn't even make that big of news  like it made news but it wasn't  that big so think about the degree to  which things have  slid over the last many years now former  federal prosecutor renato marriotti who  has been a guest on the show  had a good twitter thread about the  meaning of all of this and just a few  points  that renato makes one quote the mere  fact that a special grand jury was  impaneled  does not mean that any particular person  will be charged it does not necessarily  mean that trump himself will be charged  but it is fair to say  that vance's investigation is far along  and that  charges are on the horizon does not mean  it will be against trump  number two when it comes to trump  himself in cases like this  it's often about what you can prove  trump knew  when you're talking about this type of  fraud in white collar crime and renato  tweets quote  whenever i investigated tax or fraud  cases the case came down to whether we  had sufficient proof of the defendant's  knowledge of the false statements  contained in the documents  that state of mind is what distinguishes  fr